tial equation combined with only one condition.\n\n- The second system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$ and $x=3$).\n\n- The third system is not a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation combined with only one condition." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338587/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34d342c-e7fc-581b-b3d1-ed6a49f1a62f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338587"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130997/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "990550c2-1f66-57b6-a808-87a7250d51f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130997/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "8bc8f8be-1c2f-590b-9aaa-a20c5b9b8b69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130997/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "88cb597e-8149-548e-b5e5-186da4c49ab8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130997/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "979d7ba2-e076-5fa9-8f2e-7c1591690975" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130997/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "773c8a77-ca48-5df4-8096-a9ff1e623b26" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130997/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "25b03586-b4d5-5ac9-a065-01aaeac80593" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130997/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-130997/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-130997/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-130997/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-130997/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-130997/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130997" :question/id #uuid "41bb21e9-bc52-542d-b300-e51317f5152f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130997" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+y=x,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1$\n- ${y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=xy,\\,y(0)=3,\\,y(1)=4$\n- $2{y}^{″}+{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=1$" :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is combined with two conditions, but both conditions are given at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$). This is an **initial value problem.**\n\n- The second system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$).\n\n- The third system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$ and $x=2$)." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130997/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34d342c-e7fc-581b-b3d1-ed6a49f1a62f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130997"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65012/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "92f8c785-d2a8-5cc6-a923-be3ef742cb4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65012/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "311155d6-9078-53d5-9a25-a2ab9b8aeafb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65012/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "4de5d30c-708b-5a97-be8c-cea258069384" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65012/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "dcf4da98-01fd-5632-9e6a-13177b792217" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65012/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "0451531a-2007-5cbc-a2bd-10c48330c2a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65012/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc82494-8f15-560f-a860-13defea63c40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65012/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-65012/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-65012/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-65012/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-65012/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-65012/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65012" :question/id #uuid "b765011e-9d19-55a7-93ef-fd380a1d1bd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-65012" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+4x{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=3$\n- $4{y}^{″}+y=0$\n- $x{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-y=0,\\,y(0)=-4,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-4$" :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is combined with two conditions, but both conditions are given at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$). This is an **initial value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$)." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-65012/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34d342c-e7fc-581b-b3d1-ed6a49f1a62f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65012"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338539/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f1419cb2-640d-520f-82a6-4ef1d37dc285" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338539/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ecf2f38c-f389-5b10-be05-9732fa0d4b4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338539/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "72ac967b-d7c8-5834-a10c-db6d64233911" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338539/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "11fdd2a9-be14-5aee-92fe-83b87f72059e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338539/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2d18a47e-7450-578d-8420-33647e7bfc84" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338539/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e7be93f-c30a-56db-a257-8a212ea5fec3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338539/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-338539/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-338539/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-338539/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-338539/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-338539/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338539" :question/id #uuid "ea74b3f8-211c-564a-bc78-9db82800d661" :question/math-academy-id "q-338539" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+y=x{e}^{x},\\,y(0)=3,\\,y(4)=3$\n- ${y}^{″}-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+4y=0,\\,y(-2)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(-2)=0$" :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=4$).\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the *same* location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-2$). This is an **initial value problem.**" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338539/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34d342c-e7fc-581b-b3d1-ed6a49f1a62f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338539"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338604/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" :answer/id #uuid "3f8fb82b-c972-5d5a-aec2-19969c660638" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Other" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338604/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer/id #uuid "301ed1d9-2197-53db-b3f2-a402271a852a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dirichlet" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338604/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" :answer/id #uuid "9813dbba-619a-5d70-9654-ea592aa836b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Robin" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338604/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" :answer/id #uuid "bec83c48-bb8b-5247-aa44-aeb84bbd7a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Periodic" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338604/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer/id #uuid "b2713c9f-3a49-587b-9b8f-072c0983d68e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Neumann" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338604/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed8067c2-2b57-5ebe-8fdb-ba721f50352b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338604/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer-field/choices ["q-338604/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" "q-338604/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" "q-338604/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" "q-338604/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" "q-338604/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338604" :question/id #uuid "19ed2937-5c7c-51e2-b78a-b201daf55ffb" :question/math-academy-id "q-338604" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-3{y}^{′}(x)+2y(x)={e}^{x},\\,y(0)=1,\\,y(2)=5,\\,0\\le x\\le 2\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=0$ and $x=b=2.$\n\n$$\ny(0)=1,\\,y(2)=5\n$$\n\nThese are Dirichlet boundary conditions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338604/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8c898fc-6802-5296-9866-c844f9ed0349"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338604"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338616/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" :answer/id #uuid "2ace0328-0064-54a6-a5f1-69959d3b1c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Other" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338616/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" :answer/id #uuid "075c1a4b-d8c5-5174-ac4e-484282bb60c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Periodic" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338616/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer/id #uuid "fd3cd4f1-3833-53c4-86d1-fb31a5ac0032" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Neumann" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338616/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer/id #uuid "68ac1ed9-865e-59dd-8c6b-50945bfb3fa2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dirichlet" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338616/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" :answer/id #uuid "edfead6c-ed78-5eb2-a8a5-9e52f7c80935" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Robin" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338616/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fce5b5d-317e-5505-9d2c-fbf88137908f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338616/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer-field/choices ["q-338616/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" "q-338616/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" "q-338616/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" "q-338616/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" "q-338616/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338616" :question/id #uuid "86c65f90-930e-573c-bc91-15e1b7a5fd16" :question/math-academy-id "q-338616" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+{y}^{′}(x)={x}^{3},\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-3,\\,-1\\le x\\le 2\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=-1$ and $x=b=2.$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-3\n$$\n\nThese are Neumann boundary conditions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338616/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8c898fc-6802-5296-9866-c844f9ed0349"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338616"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338612/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" :answer/id #uuid "07cf1745-beb5-5399-8fe1-e95e04cbb6f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Periodic" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338612/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer/id #uuid "557d495d-2e4d-54ac-915a-3d4f19b4109e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dirichlet" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338612/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" :answer/id #uuid "23cee097-bcd4-5ece-a467-52e2db295e2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Robin" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338612/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" :answer/id #uuid "de61f7eb-0f48-5fd5-b810-9838a794b50a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Other" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338612/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer/id #uuid "d69a6b24-b747-5f27-b3a4-697f52d29fc2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Neumann" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338612/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a44d2702-406a-58cf-ab76-e0745b39fc2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338612/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer-field/choices ["q-338612/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" "q-338612/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" "q-338612/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" "q-338612/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" "q-338612/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338612" :question/id #uuid "a8c9b8ab-cb77-521a-9c0d-45131dd26b98" :question/math-academy-id "q-338612" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-y(x)={e}^{-x},\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(5)=0,\\,1\\le x\\le 5\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=1$ and $x=b=5.$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(5)=0\n$$\n\nThese are Neumann boundary conditions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338612/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8c898fc-6802-5296-9866-c844f9ed0349"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338602/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" :answer/id #uuid "3607a124-e398-59d5-9e5b-0bd7aafeef3e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Other" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338602/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" :answer/id #uuid "64cf105c-6c18-558f-8bbe-d7e301d35ff0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Periodic" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338602/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer/id #uuid "228bb783-dbe2-5726-a5db-04c782b98e98" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Neumann" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338602/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" :answer/id #uuid "ebf270f3-dab7-51b2-ad65-00b227744574" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Robin" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338602/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer/id #uuid "1dab97cc-9221-5723-8759-17619e27e880" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dirichlet" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338602/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f48ca847-3d03-5209-87fe-f76dd2702dfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338602/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer-field/choices ["q-338602/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" "q-338602/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" "q-338602/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" "q-338602/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" "q-338602/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338602" :question/id #uuid "8943ad3a-c60a-5a9d-ace9-073cae5be3c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-338602" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+4y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\,y(-1)=2,\\,y(3)=-1,\\,-1\\le x\\le 3\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=-1$ and $x=b=3.$\n\n$$\ny(-1)=2,\\,y(3)=-1\n$$\n\nThese are Dirichlet boundary conditions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338602/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8c898fc-6802-5296-9866-c844f9ed0349"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338602"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338614/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" :answer/id #uuid "00203c81-c162-5402-acf3-f76228be8e5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Robin" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338614/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer/id #uuid "a03252fe-7602-5f5d-8eec-365d26365cc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dirichlet" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338614/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" :answer/id #uuid "477710c9-ad27-5403-ba5e-f3e09e5c9c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Other" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338614/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" :answer/id #uuid "d0aa291a-644a-518b-b681-1533efcec49f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Periodic" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338614/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer/id #uuid "ad65abd1-a297-5d67-a597-f05bff1ce68c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Neumann" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338614/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29db159e-d61d-51c9-99df-156a784f7842" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338614/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer-field/choices ["q-338614/selection/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" "q-338614/selection/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" "q-338614/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" "q-338614/selection/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" "q-338614/selection/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338614" :question/id #uuid "a744fa75-b90f-5f73-b368-4c9555f9e712" :question/math-academy-id "q-338614" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+9y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\,{y}^{′}(0)=4,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=4,\\,0\\le x\\le 3\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=0$ and $x=b=3.$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=4,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=4\n$$\n\nThese are Neumann boundary conditions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338614/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8c898fc-6802-5296-9866-c844f9ed0349"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338614"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "eef90cbe-f550-50b4-b701-f3686d9f4400" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "80a283bc-b73b-53f0-aff9-6867d2e2cea7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba4f9ae4-3d97-5642-976b-112fbada5932" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338714/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-338714/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338714/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-2/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" :answer/id #uuid "c87c88a8-2547-574d-ace4-16647691adde" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Robin" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-2/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer/id #uuid "cb9ec732-5ccd-563a-99f8-099ffa715740" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Neumann" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-2/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer/id #uuid "57827cd0-34e8-5f40-a6d9-47b34a8f6cdf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Dirichlet" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f08eaf3b-4881-5bda-b0e0-76d8ec093730" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338714/field-2/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" :answer-field/choices ["q-338714/field-2/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" "q-338714/field-2/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" "q-338714/field-2/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-3/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "39376374-8e75-55d9-b3f0-a0fc38e2cd74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-3/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "300d05f8-f552-5ccc-b4ca-d7a837240de8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a0537a0-53c5-5377-a7c8-57f713ad1c6a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338714/field-3/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-338714/field-3/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" "q-338714/field-3/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-4/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "10a6fea3-1839-5830-92b7-55eeca38cd32" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-4/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "9390a4d5-5ba8-54a8-b30d-ede76edaee65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "309372f7-eed8-552e-af7e-0da285f84970" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338714/field-4/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-338714/field-4/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338714/field-4/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338714" :question/id #uuid "3236c2c3-70e6-5ffe-8ec5-9cf7dde62c74" :question/math-academy-id "q-338714" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+x{y}^{′}(x)+y(x)={x}^{2}+1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi \n$$\n\n$$\ny(0)=1,\\,y(\\pi )=0\n$$\n\nComplete the missing information below:\n\n$\\,$ The governing differential equation is {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, the {{field-2}} boundary conditions are {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nA set of Dirichlet, Neumann, or Robin boundary conditions is homogeneous if both right-hand sides are zero (i.e., ${\\gamma }_{1}={\\gamma }_{2}=0.)$ Otherwise, they are inhomogeneous.\n\nA boundary value problem is homogeneous if the differential equation is homogeneous $(f≡0)$ and the corresponding boundary conditions are homogeneous. Otherwise, the BVP is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- The governing differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+x{y}^{′}(x)+y(x)={x}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side $f(x)={x}^{2}+1≢0,$ the equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$\n\n- The boundary conditions are\n\n$$\ny(0)=1,\\,y(\\pi )=0.\n$$\n\nThese are $\\text{Dirichlet}$ boundary conditions, and since the right-hand sides are not zero for both, they are $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$\n\n- Since the governing equation is inhomogeneous, and the boundary conditions are inhomogeneous, the BVP is $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338714/field-1" "q-338714/field-2" "q-338714/field-3" "q-338714/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af8cf798-4327-5f5b-82ab-f622f20ccc38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338714"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338697/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "d1bad883-f5ff-548b-a641-b3c4ff2b4e12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338697/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "2ae0f690-65f1-503d-87ba-477da0971632" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338697/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3baceb0-bf2c-52ba-a667-dc0f23f260f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338697/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-338697/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" "q-338697/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40