er-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338715" :question/id #uuid "b958564a-16d6-57b6-bb41-e2a011ee61b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-338715" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{y}^{′}(x)+2y(x)={e}^{x},\\,0\\le x\\le 2\n$$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-3\n$$\n\nComplete the missing information below:\n\n$\\,$ The governing differential equation is {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, the {{field-2}} boundary conditions are {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nA set of Dirichlet, Neumann, or Robin boundary conditions is homogeneous if both right-hand sides are zero (i.e., ${\\gamma }_{1}={\\gamma }_{2}=0.)$ Otherwise, they are inhomogeneous.\n\nA boundary value problem is homogeneous if the differential equation is homogeneous $(f≡0)$ and the corresponding boundary conditions are homogeneous. Otherwise, the BVP is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- The governing differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{y}^{′}(x)+2y(x)={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side $f(x)={e}^{x}≢0,$ the equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$\n\n- The boundary conditions are\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-3.\n$$\n\nThese are $\\text{Neumann}$ boundary conditions, and since the right-hand sides are not zero for both, they are $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$\n\n- Since the governing equation is inhomogeneous, and the boundary conditions are inhomogeneous, the BVP is $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338715/field-1" "q-338715/field-2" "q-338715/field-3" "q-338715/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af8cf798-4327-5f5b-82ab-f622f20ccc38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338713/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "1aff92f9-b115-5d80-af7a-5ea17d6d94cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338713/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "bdef89e8-e9ad-566f-9843-a5925df79237" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338713/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a89853aa-7706-57e7-80f9-49f5fce2a3a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338713/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-338713/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" "q-338713/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338713/field-2/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" :answer/id #uuid "9efda2ed-b54b-526d-aeab-d22dac6f62cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Neumann" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338713/field-2/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" :answer/id #uuid "33e1555a-89b0-52be-ab9a-c05bc0f7e670" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Robin" :db/